    skos:relatedMatch elter:10021 .

nma-resourcetypes:d97f-vb57 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broadMatch fabio-docs:d4e2568 ;
    skos:broader nma-resourcetypes:c_efa0 ;
    skos:definition "A commentary is a more in-depth analysis written to draw attention to a work already published. Commentaries are somewhat like “reviews” in that the author presents his or her analysis of a work and why it  would be of interest to a specific audience. [Source: https://www.enago.com/academy/perspective-opinion-and-commentary-pieces]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch coar-resource-type:D97F-VB57 ;
    skos:inScheme nma-resourcetypes: ;
    skos:notation "d97f-vb57"^^nma-vocabularies:invenioid ;
    skos:prefLabel "commentary"@en .

nma-resourcetypes:dd58-gfsx a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader nma-resourcetypes:dataset ;
    skos:definition "Data resulting from assessing specific properties (or characteristics) of beings, things, phenomena, (and/ or processes) by applying pre-established standards and/or specialized instruments or techniques. [Source: Adapted from  https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_3.0.html]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch coar-resource-type:DD58-GFSX ;
    skos:inScheme nma-resourcetypes: ;
    skos:notation "dd58-gfsx"^^nma-vocabularies:invenioid ;
    skos:prefLabel "measurement and test data"@en ;
    skos:relatedMatch elter:10017 .

nma-resourcetypes:dx5j-ta9r a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broadMatch mesh:D000078182,
        fabio-docs:d4e5605 ;
    skos:broader nma-resourcetypes:publication-report ;
    skos:definition "In the context of systematic reviews and meta-analyses, a protocol is a document that presents an explicit plan for a systematic review. The protocol details the rationale and a priori methodological and analytical approach of the review. https://www.bmj.com/content/349/bmj.g7647"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "New concept included t be added to upcoming version 4.0"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch coar-resource-type:DX5J-TA9R ;
    skos:inScheme nma-resourcetypes: ;
    skos:notation "dx5j-ta9r"^^nma-vocabularies:invenioid ;
    skos:prefLabel "knowledge synthesis protocol"@en .

nma-resourcetypes:ff4c-28rk a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader nma-resourcetypes:dataset ;
    skos:definition "Data resulting from observational research, which involves collecting observations as they occur (for example, observing behaviors, events, development of condition or disease, etc.), without attempting to manipulate any of the independent variables. [Source:  Adapted from https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_3.0.html]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Data resulting from observational research, which involves collecting observations as they occur (for example, observing behaviors, events, development of condition or disease, etc.), without attempting to manipulate any of the independent variables. [Source:  Adapted from https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_3.0.html]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch coar-resource-type:FF4C-28RK ;
    skos:inScheme nma-resourcetypes: ;
    skos:narrowMatch elter:10018 ;
    skos:notation "ff4c-28rk"^^nma-vocabularies:invenioid ;
    skos:prefLabel "observational data"@en .

nma-resourcetypes:fxf3-d3g7 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broadMatch datacite-v4.4:Dataset ;
    skos:broader nma-resourcetypes:dataset ;
    skos:definition "Data collected or assembled from multiple, often heterogeneous sources that have one or more reference points in common, and at least one of the sources was originally produced for other purposes. The data are incorporated in a new entity. For example, providing data on the number of universities in the last 150 years using a variety of available sources (e.g. finance documents, official statistics, university registers), combining survey data with information about geographical areas from official statistics (e.g. population density, doctors per capita, etc.), or using RSS to collect blog posts or tweets, etc. [Source: Adapted from https://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CV/ModeOfCollection_3.0.html]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch coar-resource-type:FXF3-D3G7 ;
    skos:inScheme nma-resourcetypes: ;
    skos:notation "fxf3-d3g7"^^nma-vocabularies:invenioid ;
    skos:prefLabel "compiled data"@en .

nma-resourcetypes:gpq7-g5ve a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader nma-resourcetypes:publication-patent ;
    skos:definition "Plant variety protection, also called a \"plant breeder's right\" (PBR), is a form of intellectual property right granted to the breeder of a new plant variety . According to this right, certain acts concerning the exploitation of the protected variety require the prior authorization of the breeder. Plant variety protection is an independent sui generis form of protection, tailored to protect new plant varieties and has certain features in common with other intellectual property rights. [Source: https://www.wipo.int/edocs/pubdocs/en/wipo_pub_943_2018.pdf]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch coar-resource-type:GPQ7-G5VE ;
    skos:inScheme nma-resourcetypes: ;
    skos:notation "gpq7-g5ve"^^nma-vocabularies:invenioid ;
    skos:prefLabel "plant variety protection"@en .

nma-resourcetypes:h41y-fw7b a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader nma-resourcetypes:dataset ;
    skos:definition "A laboratory notebook (colloq. lab notebook or lab book) is a primary record of research. Researchers use a lab notebook to document their hypotheses, experiments and initial analysis or interpretation of these experiments. This label is used both for traditional and electronic laboratory notebook. [Source: Adapted from https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lab_notebook]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch coar-resource-type:H41Y-FW7B ;
    skos:inScheme nma-resourcetypes: ;
    skos:narrowMatch datacite-v4.4:ComputationalNotebook ;
    skos:notation "h41y-fw7b"^^nma-vocabularies:invenioid ;
    skos:prefLabel "laboratory notebook"@en .

nma-resourcetypes:jbnf-dyad a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broadMatch <https://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/ncimbrowser/ConceptReport.jsp?dictionary=NCI%20Metathesaurus&code=C1707689> ;
    skos:broader nma-resourcetypes:542x-3s04 ;
    skos:definition "Industrial designs are applied to a wide variety of industrial products and handicrafts. They refer to the ornamental or aesthetic aspects of a useful article,including compositions of lines or colors or any three-dimensional forms that give a special appearance to a product or handicraft. [Source: https://www.wipo.int/edocs/pubdocs/en/wipo_pub_943_2018.pdf]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch coar-resource-type:JBNF-DYAD ;
    skos:inScheme nma-resourcetypes: ;
    skos:notation "jbnf-dyad"^^nma-vocabularies:invenioid ;
    skos:prefLabel "industrial design"@en .

nma-resourcetypes:mw8g-3cr8 a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broadMatch datacite-v4.4:Software,
        fabio-docs:d4e4551 ;
    skos:broader nma-resourcetypes:publication-patent ;
    skos:definition "In order to obtain a patent, a software invention must not fall under other non-patentable subject matter (for example, abstract ideas or mathematical theories) and has to fulfill the other substantive patentability criteria (for example, novelty, inventive step [non-obviousness] and industrial applicability [usefulness]). [Source: https://www.wipo.int/patents/en/faq_patents.html]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch coar-resource-type:MW8G-3CR8 ;
    skos:inScheme nma-resourcetypes: ;
    skos:notation "mw8g-3cr8"^^nma-vocabularies:invenioid ;
    skos:prefLabel "software patent"@en .

nma-resourcetypes:nhd0-w6sy a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broadMatch datacite-v4.4:Dataset ;
    skos:broader nma-resourcetypes:dataset ;
    skos:definition "Data resulting from a survey, which is defined as an investigation about the characteristics of a given population by means of collecting data from a sample of that population and estimating their characteristics through the systematic use of statistical methodology. Included are censuses, sample surveys, the collection of data from administrative records and derived statistical activities as well as questionnaires. [Source: Adapted from https://stats.oecd.org/glossary/detail.asp?ID=2620]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch coar-resource-type:NHD0-W6SY ;
    skos:inScheme nma-resourcetypes: ;
    skos:notation "nhd0-w6sy"^^nma-vocabularies:invenioid ;
    skos:prefLabel "survey data"@en .

nma-resourcetypes:qh80-2r4e a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader nma-resourcetypes:software ;
    skos:definition "Source code is any collection of code, with or without comments, written using a human-readable programming language, usually as plain text. [Source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Source_code]"@en ;
